### Page 1 of 1

```text
MEMORANDUM

TO:

Mayor Rick Kaysen

Members of the City Council

FROM:

Vicki Nemecek, Assistant Public Works Director

DATE:

June 4, 2014

SUBJECT:

Announcement of a Public Hearing to be held June 23, 2014 at 6:00
pm in City Council Chambers, 2101 O’Neil Avenue, Cheyenne, Wyoming, to receive public
comments regarding the intent of the City of Cheyenne to designate the use of Excess
Monies from the 2011 through 2014 Optional One Percent Sales Tax for Right-of-Way
Maintenance, for the Lake Minnehaha Phase I Project, and for Prioritized Energy
Efficiency Projects in City-owned facilities.
________________________________________________________________________
Resolution #5224 describes use of the 2011 through 2014 One Percent Sales Tax. It designates
80% of Excess Monies (funds collected over the estimate of $40 Million) toward Street and
Road Maintenance and Construction Projects and 10% of Excess Monies are directed to Human
Services. The remaining 10% remains undesignated. We anticipate the undesignated 10% of
Excess Monies to be approximately $863,119.

Parks and Recreation is in need of $371,000 to perform essential right-of-way maintenance
throughout the City. These funds would pay for routine upkeep, preservation, and replacement of
landscape enhanced City rights-of-way. Costs include equipment, materials, supplies, and labor
for tree pruning, tree replacement, snow removal, mowing, weed control, debris removal, and
irrigation.

Parks and Recreation is also in need of $129,000 to fund a portion of the Lake Minnehaha Phase
I Project. This project was funded with SLIB Consensus funds; however, actual costs exceeded
estimates once the project was fully designed and contracted.

We recommend designating any remaining Excess Monies, estimated at $363,119, to Public
Works for completion of energy efficiency projects in priority order and as funds allow. The top
priority would be to upgrade lighting in areas that were not included in the ARRA Grant funded
lighting project. There were insufficient funds to complete lighting upgrades in all areas of our
facilities. In addition, there are several garage doors and HVAC systems in need of replacement
that would improve energy efficiency in those facilities.

Resolution #5224 states that undesignated excess monies shall be spent for such purposes as may
be approved by the governing body following a public hearing.

City staff recommends adoption of the resolution.
```
